This PR makes the `.well-known/agent-card.json` URL optional when hosting an A2A agent by separating it from the core JSON-RPC functionality.

## Problem

Previously, the `MapA2A` method automatically mapped both the JSON-RPC endpoint and the well-known agent discovery endpoint:

```csharp
app.MapA2A(taskManager, "/agent");
// This mapped BOTH:
// - POST /agent (JSON-RPC endpoint) 
// - GET /.well-known/agent.json (agent discovery)
```

This forced all A2A agents to expose discovery information, even when it wasn't desired for security or architectural reasons.

## Solution

Split the functionality into two separate extension methods:

```csharp
// Option 1: JSON-RPC only (no agent discovery)
app.MapA2A(taskManager, "/agent");

// Option 2: Agent discovery only
app.MapWellKnownAgentCard(taskManager, "/agent");

// Option 3: Both (maintains previous behavior)
app.MapA2A(taskManager, "/agent");
app.MapWellKnownAgentCard(taskManager, "/agent");
```

## Changes Made

- **Modified `MapA2A`**: Removed the well-known endpoint mapping, now only handles JSON-RPC
- **Added `MapWellKnownAgentCard`**: New extension method that maps only the `/.well-known/agent.json` endpoint
- **Updated samples**: All sample applications now explicitly call both methods to preserve existing functionality
- **Added comprehensive tests**: New test suite validates independent operation of both methods

## Benefits

- **Flexibility**: Developers can choose whether to expose agent discovery
- **Security**: Agents can be hosted without exposing discovery information
- **Backward compatibility**: Existing behavior is preserved by calling both methods
- **Separation of concerns**: JSON-RPC handling and agent discovery are now logically separate

This approach follows the pattern used by other A2A implementations and provides the granular control requested in the issue.

Fixes #105.

