## Problem

The `updateChartData` function was duplicated identically in both `createGameBarChart` and `createGameBarChartWithCustomFormat` functions in `stats.js`. This violated the DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principle and created maintenance overhead.

```javascript
// Duplicated in both functions:
function updateChartData() {
    // Filter data to only include visible bars
    const visibleLabels = [];
    const visibleTotals = [];
    const visibleColors = [];

    originalData.labels.forEach((label, index) => {
        if (!hiddenBars[index]) {
            visibleLabels.push(label);
            visibleTotals.push(originalData.totals[index]);
            visibleColors.push(colors[index]);
        }
    });

    return {
        labels: visibleLabels,
        totals: visibleTotals,
        colors: visibleColors
    };
}
```

## Solution

Created a shared utility function `getFilteredChartData(originalData, hiddenBars, colors)` at a higher scope and refactored both chart creation functions to use it:

```javascript
// New shared function
function getFilteredChartData(originalData, hiddenBars, colors) {
    // Filter data to only include visible bars
    const visibleLabels = [];
    const visibleTotals = [];
    const visibleColors = [];

    originalData.labels.forEach((label, index) => {
        if (!hiddenBars[index]) {
            visibleLabels.push(label);
            visibleTotals.push(originalData.totals[index]);
            visibleColors.push(colors[index]);
        }
    });

    return {
        labels: visibleLabels,
        totals: visibleTotals,
        colors: visibleColors
    };
}

// Updated local functions
function updateChartData() {
    return getFilteredChartData(originalData, hiddenBars, colors);
}
```

## Benefits

- **Eliminates code duplication**: Reduced 18 lines of duplicated logic
- **Improves maintainability**: Future changes to the filtering logic only need to be made in one place
- **Maintains functionality**: All chart interactions and legend behavior remain unchanged
- **Better code organization**: Clear separation between shared utilities and function-specific logic

## Testing

The refactored code has been verified through unit testing to ensure the chart data filtering functionality works correctly:

![Test Results](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/05d94998-1500-4ed0-aa90-a6794db154c4)

The test confirms that the shared function properly filters chart data based on hidden bars while preserving the exact same behavior as the original duplicated functions.

