This PR removes the reflection-based approach for handling Avatar Dynamics components (VRCPhysBone, VRCPhysBoneCollider, VRCContactSender, VRCContactReceiver) and replaces it with direct component usage.

## Background

The reflection wrappers were originally introduced to maintain compatibility when PhysBones were not always included in VRCSDK. However, since PhysBones are now always available in supported VRCSDK versions, this reflection layer is no longer necessary and adds unnecessary complexity and performance overhead.

## Changes

### Removed Reflection Infrastructure
- Completely removed `VRCSDKUtility.Reflection` static class containing wrapper classes:
  - `PhysBone` wrapper (85+ lines of reflection code)
  - `PhysBoneCollider` wrapper (25+ lines)
  - `ContactBase` wrapper (45+ lines)
- Removed static Type fields: `PhysBoneType`, `PhysBoneColliderType`, `ContactReceiverType`, `ContactSenderType`

### Updated Component Access
Updated methods throughout the codebase to use typed components directly:

```csharp
// Before (using reflection)
internal Component[] GetPhysBones()
{
    return AvatarDescriptor.GetComponentsInChildren(VRCSDKUtility.PhysBoneType, true);
}

// After (direct typed access)
internal VRCPhysBone[] GetPhysBones()
{
    return AvatarDescriptor.GetComponentsInChildren<VRCPhysBone>(true);
}
```

### Simplified Component Manipulation
Component operations now use direct property access instead of reflection:

```csharp
// Before (using reflection wrapper)
var boneComponent = new Reflection.PhysBone(boneObject);
if (boneComponent.Colliders[colliderIndex] == c)
{
    boneComponent.ClearCollider(colliderIndex);
}

// After (direct component access)  
if (boneObject.colliders[colliderIndex] == c)
{
    boneObject.colliders[colliderIndex] = null;
}
```

### Removed Obsolete Compatibility Code
- Removed `IsPhysBonesImported()` method and all its usages since PhysBones are always available
- Removed `PhysBonesSDKRequired` i18n entries from all language files (en-US, ja-JP, ru-RU)
- Eliminated unnecessary type casting operations where collections were already properly typed
- Removed PhysBones availability checks from UI components
- Simplified contact filtering by using `ContactBase.IsLocalOnly` directly instead of `IsLocalOnlyContact()` wrapper
- Removed the `IsLocalOnlyContact()` method entirely

## Benefits

- **Performance**: Eliminates reflection overhead during component access and manipulation
- **Type Safety**: Compile-time type checking instead of runtime reflection validation
- **Maintainability**: Removes ~200 lines of complex reflection wrapper code
- **Readability**: Direct component access is more intuitive and easier to debug
- **Future-proof**: No dependency on internal reflection implementation details

## Compatibility

This change maintains full functional compatibility - the same Avatar Dynamics components are used, just accessed directly instead of through reflection wrappers. All existing functionality remains intact while being more efficient and maintainable.

Fixes #123.

